WEBVTT

00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:05.320
No matter what knitting patterns you use,
adjusting the length of your

00:00:05.386 --> 00:00:07.210
sleeves isn't difficult.

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:12.490
Use the Knit It Now Magic formula
tool and let us do the math for you.

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:16.610
I want to make my sleeve three
inches shorter than the pattern.

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:23.170
The original pattern length is 16.75 inches plus 2 inches for ribbing.

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:27.010
I'm going to keep my wrist measurement
the same at nine inches,

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:32.090
and I'm going to keep the upper
arm measurement the same at 14.5.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:35.570
All I want to adjust is the sleeve length.

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:42.000
I'll make it 13.75 and keep the ribbing at 2 inches.

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:46.130
I'll use the Magic Formula tool in inches.

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:50.370
Now, the shaping is going to be
for both sides of my sleeve.

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:52.840
I'll enter my gauge.

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:59.600
The starting width is the wrist
measurement of 9 inches and the ending

00:00:59.666 --> 00:01:03.570
width is the upper arm measurement of 14.5 inches.

00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:08.960
I want the shaped section
of my sleeve to be 13.75.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:11.930
Here are my knitting instructions.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:16.280
All of the increases are evenly spaced
and my sleeve will be the perfect length.

